WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.536 --> 00:00:18.897
are you doing in First City?"

2
00:00:19.157 --> 00:00:21.319
Zann asked, stunned to see Jev.

3
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.341
Jev ignored the question.

4
00:00:23.361 --> 00:00:26.664
"It's a new kind of magic," he said with a smirk.

5
00:00:26.684 --> 00:00:30.988
"Your parents aren't the only ones who can invent stuff, you know."

6
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.462
"Huh?" Zann was still confused by his old enemy's unexpected appearance.

7
00:00:37.402 --> 00:00:42.304
He glanced at Zing, who was flying overhead, whistling suspiciously at Jev.

8
00:00:43.225 --> 00:00:44.525
"What are you talking about?

9
00:00:45.105 --> 00:00:45.986
What new magic?"

10
00:00:46.986 --> 00:00:48.126
"The image, dummy."

11
00:00:48.407 --> 00:00:49.387
Jev rolled his eyes.

12
00:00:49.407 --> 00:00:54.169
"The new magic makes the image visible to any living thing except Reds.

13
00:00:55.369 --> 00:00:56.810
See?" He stepped forward.

14
00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.251
The image appeared again.

15
00:00:59.431 --> 00:01:01.572
This time Zann was able to get a better look.

16
00:01:02.396 --> 00:01:05.118
It was an ad for the mass protest on his birthday.

17
00:01:05.138 --> 00:01:07.140
"What's the big deal?"

18
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.481
Zann said with a frown.

19
00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:11.063
"Everyone knows about that protest.

20
00:01:11.363 --> 00:01:12.564
It's been all over the news."

21
00:01:12.584 --> 00:01:17.047
"Maybe." Jev stepped back, and the ad disappeared again.

22
00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:22.071
"But the image is a good way to make it clear that Reds aren't welcome there."

23
00:01:23.072 --> 00:01:24.493
Zann's head was spinning.

24
00:01:25.454 --> 00:01:28.156
He'd been wishing all week for visitors from Swamp Bottom.

25
00:01:29.024 --> 00:01:32.686
However, Jev definitely wasn't one of the people he'd had in mind!

26
00:01:32.706 --> 00:01:37.049
"I thought the protest was to promote Void rights," Zann said.

27
00:01:37.069 --> 00:01:40.250
"Why wouldn't Voids want Reds to support that?"

28
00:01:41.111 --> 00:01:42.632
"You're so naive."

29
00:01:42.932 --> 00:01:44.132
Jev was still smirking.

30
00:01:44.152 --> 00:01:46.634
"Things are changing in Magica.

31
00:01:47.074 --> 00:01:49.816
And Reds like you probably won't like what's coming.

32
00:01:50.796 --> 00:01:53.698
That's why my parents decided to come to First City.

33
00:01:54.718 --> 00:01:57.400
We want to help Laddno bring about those changes."

34
00:01:58.488 --> 00:02:01.630
"Laddno?" Zann was surprised to hear the man's name again.

35
00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:03.892
"You've heard of Laddno?"

36
00:02:03.912 --> 00:02:06.153
"Hasn't everyone?"

37
00:02:06.333 --> 00:02:06.834
Jev said.

38
00:02:06.854 --> 00:02:10.456
"He's one of the most successful businessmen in Magica.

39
00:02:11.357 --> 00:02:12.918
He knows how to get things done.

40
00:02:13.358 --> 00:02:17.901
Including the Void rights stuff and, you know, other things.

41
00:02:19.082 --> 00:02:22.084
Now that he's involved, everything is going to change.

42
00:02:22.624 --> 00:02:24.146
Just you wait and see."

43
00:02:25.326 --> 00:02:27.388
Zann wasn't sure what Jev was talking about.

44
00:02:27.864 --> 00:02:30.585
But he didn't want to talk to his old enemy anymore.

45
00:02:30.605 --> 00:02:33.486
"Excuse me," Zann said.

46
00:02:33.506 --> 00:02:37.007
"I'm sure you don't want to be seen with a Red like me.

47
00:02:37.547 --> 00:02:38.667
So I'm out of here."

48
00:02:41.108 --> 00:02:44.109
He grabbed Zing, snapped his fingers, and zapped away.

49
00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:54.152
Splash! "Drat," Zann grumbled, realizing he'd barely stopped to think about where he wanted to land.

50
00:02:55.564 --> 00:02:58.505
He glanced around and recognized a small local park.

51
00:02:59.325 --> 00:03:04.326
Good. At least he hadn't accidentally zapped to Wormwood or some other nasty place.

52
00:03:05.447 --> 00:03:07.627
He stepped out of the small pond where he'd landed.

53
00:03:10.188 --> 00:03:12.589
Zing flew off to chase a bird in the treetops.

54
00:03:13.949 --> 00:03:15.129
Zann looked around again.

55
00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:16.910
The park was deserted.

56
00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:21.471
Zann rubbed his fingers together, preparing to zap back home.

57
00:03:22.411 --> 00:03:24.772
Then he paused and decided to wait a moment.

58
00:03:25.676 --> 00:03:28.838
Talking to Jev had made Zann curious about Laddno.

59
00:03:29.718 --> 00:03:32.020
Everyone seemed to be talking about this guy lately.

60
00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.681
Yet Zann knew almost nothing about the man.

61
00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:37.503
"I'll check the Directory," he thought.

62
00:03:38.423 --> 00:03:43.847
The Directory listed the names of all the people in Magica, along with basic information about each of

63
00:03:43.887 --> 00:03:48.869
them. Zann rubbed his hands together again, creating more magic friction.

64
00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:52.972
A book-like magical image appeared in the air in front of him.

65
00:03:53.996 --> 00:03:56.778
Countless tiny photos floated in the image.

66
00:03:57.799 --> 00:03:59.120
"Laddno!" Zann said.

67
00:04:00.181 --> 00:04:04.765
Instantly, the photos scattered as Laddno's picture expanded to fill the screen.

68
00:04:05.946 --> 00:04:07.928
Zann scrolled quickly past the photo.

69
00:04:08.988 --> 00:04:13.012
Thanks to the ads for the protest, he already knew what Laddno looked like.

70
00:04:14.013 --> 00:04:16.395
Now he wanted information about him.

71
00:04:17.295 --> 00:04:18.476
Zann scanned the entry.

72
00:04:19.357 --> 00:04:22.720
As Jev had mentioned, Laddno was listed as being a businessman.

73
00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:28.721
Some citizens of Magica had no talent or patience for certain types of creative magic.

74
00:04:29.682 --> 00:04:35.843
So they hired people like Laddno to help them conjure a nicer house or more comfortable furniture or

75
00:04:35.943 --> 00:04:37.324
clothing that fit them properly.

76
00:04:38.324 --> 00:04:41.205
And of course, Voids couldn't create their own things at all.

77
00:04:42.165 --> 00:04:48.027
They had to rely on family members, friends, or people like Laddno to conjure all their clothes and

78
00:04:48.067 --> 00:04:48.787
other necessities.

79
00:04:49.907 --> 00:04:54.821
Zann read that Laddno had been born in First City and was a few years younger than Zann's

80
00:04:54.881 --> 00:05:00.884
parents. He was known to have fairly strong magic for a non-Red, and he currently lived in the

81
00:05:00.924 --> 00:05:02.784
wealthy neighborhood of Treeview.

82
00:05:02.804 --> 00:05:05.626
"Treeview," Zann muttered.

83
00:05:06.526 --> 00:05:07.587
"That's where Mari lives.

84
00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:08.867
Maybe she knows him."

85
00:05:09.807 --> 00:05:13.549
Next he read about Laddno's involvement in the Void rights movement.

86
00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:19.332
The Directory said he'd joined just a few weeks earlier but had quickly become the leader of the

87
00:05:19.372 --> 00:05:24.037
movement. Before closing the Directory, Zann decided to check for Wyssa.

88
00:05:24.897 --> 00:05:28.978
The last time he'd done that, her entry looked the same as it always had.

89
00:05:29.879 --> 00:05:32.239
That was shortly after she'd taken Morb away though.

90
00:05:32.259 --> 00:05:35.920
"Wyssa," Zann said.

91
00:05:36.821 --> 00:05:40.342
Laddno's page disappeared, replaced immediately with Wyssa's.

92
00:05:41.222 --> 00:05:44.623
The page had a new note: Presumed to be off-world.

93
00:05:44.643 --> 00:05:48.084
"Wow. She really is gone," Zann thought.

94
00:05:49.032 --> 00:05:50.653
"I wonder what world she's on now."

95
00:05:51.793 --> 00:05:53.194
Zann closed the Directory.

96
00:05:53.214 --> 00:05:57.936
"Come on, Zing," he called to the dragon, who was still sniffing around in the treetops.

97
00:05:59.056 --> 00:06:01.257
"Let's go home and—aah!"

98
00:06:02.278 --> 00:06:04.799
Zann's head suddenly throbbed with pain.

99
00:06:05.739 --> 00:06:08.600
He staggered back, grabbing a tree to steady himself.

100
00:06:09.541 --> 00:06:12.642
He squeezed his eyes shut and waited for the pain to pass.

101
00:06:13.582 --> 00:06:15.023
It felt like a Red Share.

102
00:06:15.403 --> 00:06:17.684
But this seemed different from previous Red Shares.

103
00:06:18.636 --> 00:06:22.578
For one thing Zann couldn't tell which Red the Share was coming from.

104
00:06:23.539 --> 00:06:26.060
He also wasn't sure which emotion had caused it.

105
00:06:26.901 --> 00:06:27.501
Was it pain?

106
00:06:28.281 --> 00:06:29.642
Fear? Anger?

107
00:06:30.343 --> 00:06:31.923
Or some combination of all three?

108
00:06:32.864 --> 00:06:34.465
The feeling started to subside.

109
00:06:35.425 --> 00:06:37.326
Zann breathed out with relief.

110
00:06:38.367 --> 00:06:41.649
Then he gasped as the feeling washed over him again.

111
00:06:42.649 --> 00:06:46.992
The pain wasn't quite as strong this time, but now a faint voice came with it.

112
00:06:47.913 --> 00:06:55.070
Zann couldn't tell who was speaking, but the person was saying just one word: "Help!"
